    "explanation": "To both parties: the merits here are not really in dispute, but a policy escalation limb is triggered and it replaces any money ruling.\n\nOn the merits the driver's no-show is established on the record and the rider's account does not hold up. The trip record carries the driver's 'I'm Here' marker at 2026-08-09 11:17:19, and the GPS trace (EV-GPS-03306, weight 1.0) puts him inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup radius from that same second — 42 qualifying fixes in one continuous run from 11:17:19 to 11:24:09, closest approach 0.11 m, dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0. He held position for 410 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180, no_show_threshold_sec null), so the wait expired at 11:20:19, and he terminated at 11:24:09 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. POL-NS-01 limbs (a), (b), (c) and (d) therefore all hold. The rider's 'coming down now' message at 11:19:39 did not move her: her own track runs 69 fixes between 697 m and 704 m from the pin and rider_qualifying_fix_count is 0, so POL-NS-04 limbs (a) and (b) are engaged but limb (c) is affirmatively failed and the clause cannot exonerate her. POL-NS-03 does not apply (the driver was inside the arrival radius, not at a wrong face of the venue, and registered_pickup_points is 1), POL-NS-05 does not apply (the arrival marker is not false — the driver was at the pin when he tapped), and POL-NS-06 does not apply (the shortfall is -230 seconds, a surplus, not a shortfall; the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-03306-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT, carries nothing and its accumulation limb is not needed). On those findings POL-NS-07 would pay the driver 80% of the SGD 4.50 fee in force, i.e. SGD 3.60, and the rider would be left bearing the charge.\n\nThat is what the record shows, but it is not what this ruling can order. POL-NS-09(d) is engaged: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 3 for the trailing 30 days, the '3 or more' threshold, and POL-GEN-01 names that counter — and only that counter — as citable for this test. The lifetime prior_no_show_flags figure (also 3) is not used and may not be substituted for it; both advocates correctly relied on the trailing-window field and merely flagged the other. Escalation under POL-NS-09 is mandatory and terminal: it replaces the ruling, so I refund nothing to the rider and I order no compensation to the driver. The disputed SGD 4.50 is held rather than collected or refunded while review is pending.\n\nOpen question for the human reviewer: whether the rider's three no-show disputes in the trailing 30 days indicate abuse on her side, and, if it does not, whether the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee stands and the driver's SGD 3.60 entitlement under POL-NS-07 is released to him. The established POL-NS-01 findings and the SGD 3.60 figure travel with this packet. No clause produces a referral in this case: POL-NS-05(ii) is not engaged (the arrival marker is genuine), and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming branch does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d is 0, and 0 of 60 completed trips is 0.0), so its packet instruction does not fire. Confidence is 0.90; the deciding fact for the escalation sits on EV-RPROF-03306 at weight 1.0, so no impaired artifact caps it."
