    "explanation": "To both parties: this case goes to a human reviewer, and the disputed SGD 4.50 no-show fee is held — neither collected from the rider nor refunded — while that review is pending. No money moves today.\n\nOn the merits the driver's account is borne out by the record. The trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 2026-08-09 11:17:19, and the GPS trace places his first qualifying in-geofence fix at the same second, 0.11 m from the pickup pin, well inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius (POL-NS-02). He then held position for one continuous 410-second run on 42 qualifying fixes, 11:17:19 to 11:24:09 — 230 seconds more than the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; no_show_threshold_sec is null). He cancelled at 11:24:09 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the required dwell had elapsed at 11:20:19. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 therefore hold, and on those facts POL-NS-07 would pay the driver 80% of the SGD 4.50 fee — SGD 3.60, the figure the fare ledger itself computes as driver_compensation. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0, below the 4-or-more limb, and 0 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d (60) is 0.0, below the 0.08 rate limb.\n\nThe rider's grounds do not change that outcome on the merits. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate her: her own track carries 69 fixes between 697 m and 704 m from the pin with rider_qualifying_fix_count of 0 against the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, so limb (c) fails and the clause does not apply. The POL-NS-06 shortfall route is closed: the 410-second dwell exceeds the 180-second minimum, so the derived shortfall is -230 seconds and there is nothing to refund. POL-NS-06(i) accumulation was in any event unavailable — the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-03306-01 is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) and the trace shows only one in-geofence interval — but the driver does not need that limb. POL-NS-05 does not apply: the arrival marker coincides with the first in-geofence fix 0.11 m from the pin, so it is not a false marker and the waiting clock needs no recomputation. No artifact meets a POL-NS-08(a)–(d) integrity defect: the trace is 100% covered at a 10-second cadence with max_gap_sec 0.0, the chat log holds exactly the 2 messages trip_record.chat_message_count records with the msg_id sequence intact, and the SGD 4.50 fare line reconciles with the net fee in force.\n\nBut the case does not end on the merits. POL-NS-09(d) is engaged: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 3, and that limb escalates at 3 or more. That is the trailing-30-day counter the limb actually names; the lifetime prior_no_show_flags figure on the same profile is context only under POL-GEN-01 and neither side may use it as a ground, and neither did. The driver's claim for DRIVER_COMPENSATION of SGD 3.60 is well founded but is superseded by this mandatory escalation: under POL-GEN-03 escalation is terminal, it replaces the money ruling, so no refund issues and the SGD 3.60 payout is not made now. The rider's request that the SGD 4.50 be seen by a person before it is taken succeeds to this extent — the fee is frozen rather than charged. The open question for the reviewer is whether the rider's three no-show disputes in 30 days indicate abuse, and, if not, whether the verified no-show fee and the driver's SGD 3.60 entitlement should be released as the record supports. No referral is issued: no clause in this category produces one on these facts — POL-NS-05(ii) is not engaged because qualifying in-geofence fixes do exist, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming branch did not trip, so its instruction to the reviewer does not arise. The escalation packet carries both advocate briefs, the admissibility report, the clause IDs relied on and this reasoning. For routing: any released compensation (SGD 3.60) would sit below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold."
