    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the disputed SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee on TRP-03306 is placed on hold and the case goes to human review under POL-NS-09(d). No money moves on this ruling.\n\nThe merits run for the driver. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in all four limbs on the driver's evidence. (a) EV-TRIP-03306 carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 11:17:19. (b) EV-GPS-03306 places him 0.111 m from the pickup pin at that timestamp, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. (c) he held position inside the geofence for one continuous run of 410 s (42 qualifying fixes, 11:17:19 to 11:24:09), exceeding the 180 s free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; no_show_threshold_sec null). (d) he terminated at 11:24:09 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, 230 s after the dwell elapsed, with no boarding event. POL-NS-05 does not fire: the marker is not false, the driver being 0.111 m from the pin and stationary at the arrival timestamp. POL-NS-03 does not open, because the stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, not outside it, and registered_pickup_points is 1. POL-NS-06's shortfall route is closed: the 410 s dwell exceeds the 180 s minimum by 230 s, and the accumulation limb (i) has nothing to operate on because the trace shows a single in-geofence interval and EV-ADVIS-03306-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT).\n\nThe rider's own contact claim under POL-NS-04 is engaged at limbs (a) and (b) - she sent 'coming down now' at 11:19:39 and the driver neither replied within 120 s nor placed an in-app call - but limb (c) is affirmatively failed: her device never came closer than 697.09 m to the pin across 69 fixes (rider_qualifying_fix_count 0 against the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius), so POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate her and the fee falls to be decided under POL-NS-01. Her account that she was 'only a few minutes late' is not consistent with her own track.\n\nNo POL-NS-08 integrity defect is present. Limb (a): the arrival event and the first qualifying in-geofence fix share 11:17:19, i.e. 0 s of skew against the 90 s threshold. Limb (b): 100.0% coverage, 106 fixes, max_gap_sec 0.0, rider_track present. Limb (c): the chat holds exactly the 2 messages trip_record.chat_message_count records, sequence intact. Limb (d): the SGD 4.50 fee line reconciles with the net fee in force.\n\nWhy the outcome is ESCALATE and not the driver's DRIVER_COMPENSATION: POL-NS-07 would pay the driver 80% of the SGD 4.50 fee in force, i.e. SGD 3.60 - the same figure the fare ledger computes at EV-FARE-03306 - and the anti-farming check does not trip, because driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0 (below the 4-or-more limb) and 0/60 = 0.0 (below the 0.08 rate limb). But POL-NS-09(d) is independently engaged: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d stands at 3, and that limb escalates at 3 or more. The limb reads the trailing-30-day counter, not the lifetime prior_no_show_flags figure on the same profile, which is context-only under POL-GEN-01. Under POL-GEN-03 escalation is terminal and replaces the monetary ruling, so the fee is held rather than collected or refunded and the SGD 3.60 compensation is not paid on this ruling. Escalation is not a win for the rider: it freezes the SGD 4.50 rather than returning it.\n\nOpen questions for the reviewer, not instructions: whether the rider's 3 no-show disputes in the trailing 30 days in fact indicate abuse, and - POL-NS-01 being satisfied in full - whether the SGD 4.50 fee should be released to the driver together with the SGD 3.60 POL-NS-07 compensation (80% of the net SGD 4.50 fee in force). The monetary effect at stake, SGD 4.50, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold of POL-GEN-05, so but for the escalation it would have executed automatically on issue."
